t 6 2026...\nTropical Storm Isaias has formed as of the 09Z update. A faster\nmovement and track through AL into middle TN is now forecast,\nwhich may increase the impactful gusty wind potential as the\npotential hurricane weakens and moves rapidly northward through\nthe TN Valley Saturday. We have adjusted PoPs to account for\nearlier arrival of outer bands of rainfall Friday night due to \nthe faster movement. The faster movement may lessen residence time\nof heavy rainfall and could keep the flood risk low. \nNevertheless, will continue to message a low risk of flooding due \nto tropical rainfall associated with the system that is expected \nand with the Slight Risk issued by WPC for Days 3-4.\n\nIssued at 906 PM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nAs noted above, Tropical Storm Isaias has formed in the Gulf and \nwill be the feature of focus that will potentially impact the \nTennessee Valley this weekend. This storm is officially forecast \nto strengthen into a hurricane as it approaches the north central \nGulf Coast late Friday. As it does so (and eventually comes ashore\nFriday night into Saturday morning), it will be interacting and \neventually merging with a shortwave trough pivoting into the lower\nMississippi Valley. This should accelerate the system during the \nday on Saturday as it moves northward from the Gulf Coast into the\nMid South/Tennessee Valley by the afternoon/evening. The tropical\nwind field with this system should weaken considerably into a \nDe\n--- heavy rain char 52465 ---\nth the latest forecast information as we approach \nthe weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.LONG TERM...\n(Friday night through Tuesday)\n\nUpdate at 514 AM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026...\nTropical Storm Isaias has formed as of the 09Z update. A faster\nmovement and track through AL into middle TN is now forecast,\nwhich may increase the impactful gusty wind potential as the\npotential hurricane weakens and moves rapidly northward through\nthe TN Valley Saturday. We have adjusted PoPs to account for\near